{"timestamp":"2026-07-15T16:14:53.363Z","ordinal":2187,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f668f-3ac8-7903-9bce-1e4416307172","turn_id":"7c759b9c-8418-4193-9b33-1570726e6686","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0210a2fd-5a35-4392-b8d7-a5465f53c7a6","changes":{"/Users/zenray/.codex/skills/zenray-git-bulk-safety/SKILL.md":{"type":"delete","content":"---\nname: zenray-git-bulk-safety\ndescription: Safely repair, migrate, reindex, or bulk-upload ZenRayProgress media and manifests with Git transport instead of GitHub REST/raw requests. Use for thumbnail rollouts, shard migrations, bulk manifest changes, re-ingestion, or any operation touching more than a few GitHub files.\n---\n\n# ZenRay Git Bulk Safety\n\nUse this skill for a **bulk** ZenRayProgress media or manifest operation. Its invariant is simple: GitHub's REST API is control-plane only; Git is the data plane for large work.\n\n## Choose the transport\n\n| Work | Transport |\n|---|---|\n| One interactive browser capture | Existing app API transaction; the browser and Vercel cannot safely run the user's `gh`/Git credentials. Keep it small and bounded. |\n| Create an empty shard repository | `gh repo create` once if required, then clone/push with Git. |\n| Read, repair, move, reindex, or patch many manifests | Local clone + `git pull`, local files, `git commit`, `git push`. |\n| Push many media binaries | Local Git clone/worktree; batches around 900 MB, a new shard before 4.3 GB. |\n\nNever use `gh api`, `curl`/`fetch` to `api.github.com`, `raw.githubusercontent.com`, or GitHub Contents APIs in a per-file loop. `gh api` is REST despite its name. jsDelivr is allowed only for a small post-push sample of immutable public assets, never for enumerating manifests.\n\n## Mandatory workflow\n\n1. **Protect concurrent work.** Inspect `git status --short`, worktrees, and running jobs. Do not touch another agent's dirty files or a currently active batch.\n2. **Read locally.** Reuse the existing `zenray-data` clone when present; otherwise clone/sparse-clone it with Git. Set non-interactive Git (`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, `GIT_ASKPASS=/usr/bin/true`) and run `git pull --ff-only` before analysis.\n3. **Prove the association before writing.** Create a local table: source path, manifest path, stable identity (content hash where possible), dimensions/size, old pointer, new pointer, and action. Reject collisions and unmatched entries. Names alone are insufficient when duplicates exist.\n4. **Make the operation resumable.** Use deterministic shard paths, a checkpoint/report outside the content tree, and idempotent tests: an already-correct manifest creates no diff; an existing blob need not be uploaded again.\n5. **Commit coherently.** Stage only the operation's files, run `git diff --check`, make an intentionally generic commit message (no personal paths/names), then `git push`. On a concurrent rejection, `git pull --rebase` and retry a bounded number of times.\n6. **Verify the exact result.** Use `git show HEAD:<manifest>` for every changed schema type, `git status --short`, and one or a few pinned jsDelivr checks per shard commit. For encrypted thumbnails, verify the stored URL, IV, and declared dimensions—not just that an HTTP request returns 200.\n\n## ZenRay image invariants\n\n- New public images retain the original encrypted bytes in `cdnChunks[]` (each chunk <=19 MB) and carry `cdnRepo`, `cdnCommit`, `alg`, and `iv`.\n- Their derived WebP uses short edge <=1080 px, quality 60, no upscale. It has its **own plaintext hash**, encrypted blob, pinned `thumb` URL, `thumbIv`, `thumbW`, and `thumbH`.\n- A `cdnChunks[]` manifest with `thumbIv` but no `thumb` is invalid: there is no `cdnPath` from which the viewer can derive the thumbnail address. Repair it in the local clone, then Git commit/push.\n- A viewer never needs ffmpeg or Vercel conversion to render a correct uploaded thumbnail: the browser creates the WebP once at capture time; production only decrypts and displays it from jsDelivr.\n\n## Stop conditions\n\nStop before writes if the association table has a collision, a manifest has no verifiable original/source identity, a shard size would exceed 4.3 GB, Git authentication cannot push, or another active process owns the same files. Report the exact evidence and request direction rather than guessing.\n"},"/Users/zenray/.codex/skills/zenray-git-bulk-safety/agents/openai.yaml":{"type":"delete","content":"interface:\n  display_name: \"ZenRay Git Bulk Safety\"\n  short_description: \"Git-only bulk media changes without quota burn.\"\n  default_prompt: \"Use $zenray-git-bulk-safety to safely execute this ZenRay media or manifest bulk operation.\"\n"},"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Skills/zenray-git-bulk-safety/SKILL.md":{"type":"delete","content":"---\nname: zenray-git-bulk-safety\ndescription: Safely repair, migrate, reindex, or bulk-upload ZenRayProgress media and manifests with Git transport instead of GitHub REST/raw requests. Use for thumbnail rollouts, shard migrations, bulk manifest changes, re-ingestion, or any operation touching more than a few GitHub files.\n---\n\n# ZenRay Git Bulk Safety\n\nUse this skill for a **bulk** ZenRayProgress media or manifest operation. Its invariant is simple: GitHub's REST API is control-plane only; Git is the data plane for large work.\n\n## Choose the transport\n\n| Work | Transport |\n|---|---|\n| One interactive browser capture | Existing app API transaction; the browser and Vercel cannot safely run the user's `gh`/Git credentials. Keep it small and bounded. |\n| Create an empty shard repository | `gh repo create` once if required, then clone/push with Git. |\n| Read, repair, move, reindex, or patch many manifests | Local clone + `git pull`, local files, `git commit`, `git push`. |\n| Push many media binaries | Local Git clone/worktree; batches around 900 MB, a new shard before 4.3 GB. |\n\nNever use `gh api`, `curl`/`fetch` to `api.github.com`, `raw.githubusercontent.